  - question: "What is an Agent property in Appwrite Analytics?"
    answer: "An Agent property is built for AI agents and backend services. It leaves out browser metrics like pageviews and bounce rate, and focuses on events, runs, users, and a Models and tools card."
  - question: "How does the Models and tools card work?"
    answer: "Send a model prop when your agent calls a model, and a tool prop when it runs a tool. The card appears after the first event with either prop, and you can select any row to filter the dashboard."
  - question: "How do I group all events from one agent run together?"
    answer: "Pass the same sessionHash, such as a run ID or conversation ID, on every event in that run. Appwrite counts each run as one visit and measures Visit duration from its first event to its last."
